      "node_id": "kg_doc_6",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The flag of Hungary (Hungarian: \"Magyarország zászlaja\" ) is a horizontal tricolour of red, white and green. In this exact form, it has been the official flag of Hungary since May 23, 1957. The flag's form originates from national republican movements of the 18th and 19th centuries, while its colours are from the Middle Ages. The current Hungarian tricolour flag is the same as the republican movement flag of the United Kingdom (used since 1816).",
      "depth": 0,
